**assistant**:
> It actually **doesn’t match**: `m` is `nothing`, which Julia’s REPL displays as a blank line.
> 
> Your regex requires a blank line between fields:
> 
> ```regex
> \s*\n\s*\nDescription:
> ```
> 
> That means:
> 
> 1. optional whitespace
> 2. newline
> 3. optional whitespace
> 4. **another newline**
> 5. `Description:`
> 
> But `response1` contains only one newline:
> 
> ```text
> Name: CrossSectionalReturnModelCache
> Description: Builds ...
> ```
> 
> Use:
> 
> ```julia
> m = match(r"^Name:\s*(.+?)\s*\n\s*Description:\s*(.*)$"s, response1)
> ```
> 
> Then:
> 
> ```julia
> m.captures
> # ["CrossSectionalReturnModelCache",
> #  "Builds aligned, gap-aware ... forecasts."]
> ```
> 
> Details:
> 
> - `^Name:`: starts at the beginning with `Name:`
> - `\s*`: skips optional whitespace
> - `(.+?)`: captures the name, lazily
> - `\n\s*Description:`: finds the next line’s `Description:`
> - `(.*)`: captures the description
> - `s`: makes `.` include newline characters, useful if descriptions can span lines.
